WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.330
- I paid $300 for this box,

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:05.400
and I have no idea what's inside.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.760
And it's so heavy!

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:16.130
I'm about to buy a $300 mystery box.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:18.390
Somebody puts a bunch of stuff in a box.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.910
You have no idea what it is.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.200
You're basically paying for the

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.160
surprise of opening a box of mystery.

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:25.780
I've bought a mystery box before.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:28.440
It was a $100 mystery box.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:32.870
It was filled with what can
best be described as weird junk.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:34.590
It was exciting to open, though.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:36.910
Would it be even more exciting to

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:40.090
open an even more expensive mystery box?

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:42.980
I am hesitant to spend slash waste

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.630
even more money on another mystery box,

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:47.350
but they were, like, you got to do it.

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.190
Spend the money.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:50.440
Just to clarify, you want me to buy

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.230
an even more expensive mystery box?

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:54.063
- This is correct.

00:00:54.063 --> 00:00:56.870
- [Joanna] Even though there
might be garbage inside.

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:57.703
- Yes.

00:00:57.703 --> 00:01:00.090
- $300 is the maximum
budget I've been given.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:03.930
I've found a mystery
box that's exactly $300.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.720
I feel better knowing that

00:01:05.720 --> 00:01:08.070
some random person is getting this money,

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:09.330
and maybe they really need it.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:11.150
Maybe they have student loans.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.920
Maybe they're trying to pay their rent.

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:15.350
You're not selling mystery boxes on eBay

00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:17.270
if you don't need money.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.091
I just carried this box
up two flights of stairs,

00:01:22.091 --> 00:01:24.320
and it's very heavy.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:26.190
- $300?

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.460
Why did you spend that.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.293
- I don't know, man,

00:01:28.293 --> 00:01:30.380
you've got like, everything and anything.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:34.610
- Well, nothing living,
which you might expect.

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:36.660
- I know it said fragile, but (laughing).

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.890
- Oh, it's a mystery.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.723
- [Joanna] Yeah.

00:01:38.723 --> 00:01:41.490
- Oh, you bought $300 worth
of stuff you don't know?

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.323
- [Joanna] Yes.

00:01:42.323 --> 00:01:43.240
- And it's fragile, and
you're letting me shake it?

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.620
It says fragile.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:45.680
- [Joanna] Are you smelling it?

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.200
- You better believe I'm smelling it.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.640
- Not a bowling ball.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:49.740
- It feels like books.

00:01:49.740 --> 00:01:52.070
- My mind immediately
goes to frozen meats.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:54.940
- Skeletons, like human
skulls or something.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:57.210
- Joanna, these people
are just sharking you now.

00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:59.160
They're just, like, this girl on Buzzfeed

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.470
is going to buy this
box if I put it on eBay.

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.740
- Okay, well, I'm
terrified of what that is.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:05.190
- Oh god, okay.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.240
The person who sold
this box spray painted,

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:11.020
with gold spray paint, 300
on every side of the box,

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:14.670
to indicate the 300 actual
dollars that I spent on it.

00:02:14.670 --> 00:02:16.330
This box says fragile.

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:19.570
A lot of people have shaken it
already, so that's not great.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:21.280
I am getting nervous to open this.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:22.728
What if this is rocks?

00:02:22.728 --> 00:02:25.149
(ominous music)

00:02:25.149 --> 00:02:28.230
I think this is a box of
rocks and now I'm upset.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:29.740
Okay, you know what, we're
just going to open it.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.140
We're just going to open it.

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.250
I already feel my heart just dropping.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:40.440
There is a lot of stuff in here.

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.924
Where to even begin?

00:02:43.924 --> 00:02:45.740
(perky music)

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:49.230
Okay, magnetic oil drain plug.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:50.063
Cool.

00:02:50.063 --> 00:02:53.720
This is my new $300
best friend, tiny bear.

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.410
I honestly don't know what this is.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.555
A camouflage backpack.

00:02:58.555 --> 00:03:01.400
Oh, it smells weird.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.600
Is this a kite?

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:04.210
This is a kite.

00:03:04.210 --> 00:03:06.180
I don't know why I find that exciting.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.260
This is a 3D wooden puzzle.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.560
If you ever see a deer that
looks like this, just run away.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.490
This says ballet fun, exclamation point,

00:03:15.490 --> 00:03:17.280
but these little ballet dancers do not

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.490
look like they're having that much fun.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.520
I don't know what this
is, but the package says,

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:22.930
wow, this is amazing.

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.750
I feel like if you have to
say wow, this is amazing,

00:03:25.750 --> 00:03:28.660
on the package, it's not amazing.

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:31.740
This is sunglasses that come
in a box with doughnuts on it,

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:35.170
and that's really misleading,
in a mean way, I think.

00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:38.550
These glasses claim to be
the freshest shades on Earth,

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:41.010
so let's all be the judge
of whether that's true.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:46.390
Oh my god, what?

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.360
I think these glasses are priceless.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.780
Can sunglasses smell musty?

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.610
Yes, they can.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.070
Very musty.

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.550
What the hell?

00:03:57.550 --> 00:03:59.420
This is a Happy Meal toy,

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.470
from the movie Ice Age: Continental Drift.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.840
This is a Twix box, but I
don't think it has Twix in it.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.410
Not what I expected.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:10.520
A necklace.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.200
Oh my God.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:15.070
I didn't think it was possible for,

00:04:15.070 --> 00:04:17.200
like, jewelry to smell bad.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:21.140
This is the worst smelling
jewelry I've ever encountered.

00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:24.530
This smells like a sweaty gym.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.280
There's another necklace.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.113
Oh god.

00:04:27.113 --> 00:04:28.140
A jump drive.

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.110
This will be good in case
I time travel back to 2004.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:33.260
This is a big, weird box.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:34.700
Okay, interesting.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.760
This is an artist
rendering of John Lennon.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.150
I just saw some things
that looked like food,

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:42.610
and I got excited, but then worried

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.760
that you shouldn't eat
food out of a mystery box.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.590
At the same time, I'm kind of hungry,

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:47.970
so we're going to see how this goes.

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:51.520
There is actual candy in this mystery box.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.370
Oh, it's not expired.

00:04:53.370 --> 00:04:54.870
I'm going to see if anyone will eat these,

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.960
but I don't think you should.

00:04:56.960 --> 00:04:58.350
Do you like Sour Patch Kids?

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:59.183
- Yes.

00:04:59.183 --> 00:05:00.210
- [Joanna] Would you eat Sour Patch Kids

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.040
that came out of a mystery box?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:02.873
- No.

00:05:02.873 --> 00:05:03.791
- [Joanna] You wouldn't?

00:05:03.791 --> 00:05:04.624
- No.

00:05:04.624 --> 00:05:06.480
- [Joanna] It's still
good, expiration date wise.

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:07.616
- Well, I'm not worried about that.

00:05:07.616 --> 00:05:09.030
I'm worried about being poisoned.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:10.160
Yeah, I guess I would eat it.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:11.430
- [Joanna] Do you want those?

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:12.470
- Yeah.

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:15.120
- [Joanna] Well, will
you eat one right now?

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.110
- If I die, this is on you.

00:05:17.110 --> 00:05:18.010
- [Joanna] I know.

00:05:20.840 --> 00:05:22.200
- I'm not dead yet.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.050
- Now I feel bad that
I made Chelsea eat one,

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:26.008
so I feel like I have to eat one.

00:05:26.008 --> 00:05:28.675
(ominous music)

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:30.823
It's fine.

00:05:30.823 --> 00:05:32.470
There's still so much stuff in here.

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:33.400
Electrical tape.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.020
This is something I could actually use.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:36.240
It's a light switch cover.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:39.450
These are little ceramic dishes
with wine glasses on them,

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.390
and one is super broken.

00:05:41.390 --> 00:05:44.750
And it says cheers,
live life with abandon.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:47.730
This is a model race car
that you can build yourself.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:52.310
There is just one more thing
in this $300 mystery box,

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:56.950
and it is a ventilation fan.

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:00.350
One thing I learned today.

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.670
Will a $300 mystery box be

00:06:03.670 --> 00:06:08.130
any less musty than a $100 mystery box?

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:08.963
No.

00:06:08.963 --> 00:06:11.490
Just as musty, if not mustier.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:14.970
There was no garbage in this
box, so that's exciting.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.190
My hands are definitely
covered in mystery box grime,

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.340
and I'm excited to wash
my hands after this.

00:06:20.340 --> 00:06:22.560
If you bump up the price of a mystery box,

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:24.910
is the stuff inside going to get cooler?

00:06:24.910 --> 00:06:28.450
Probably not, but will you increase

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:32.910
your chances of getting
one very cool thing?

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.800
Maybe.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:36.420
I think the most important lesson

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.750
that a mystery box can teach you is

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:41.440
life is full of disappointments,

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:44.170
often brought on by yourself.

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.450
I just washed my hands after touching

00:06:46.450 --> 00:06:48.950
everything in the
mystery box, and no joke.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:51.130
The water turned gray.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:55.130
So that was crusty stuff.

00:06:55.130 --> 00:06:57.570
We all want to know what's inside a box.

